1
00:00:00,860 --> 00:00:02,640
Wealth. Fame. Power.

2
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:04,577
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:07,197
attained this and everything
else the world had to offer,

4
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:10,456
and his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:11,955
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:13,420
You can have it.

7
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:16,620
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

8
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:19,060
Now you just have to find it.

9
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:24,237
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

10
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:26,757
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine.

11
00:00:26,840 --> 00:00:29,517
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era.

12
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:35,160
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

13
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:40,440
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

14
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:42,700
One piece.

15
00:00:47,980 --> 00:00:52,697
Compass left behind,
it'll only slow us down.

16
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:58,457
Your heart will be your guide,
raise the sails and take the helm.

17
00:00:58,540 --> 00:01:01,137
That legendary place.

18
00:01:01,220 --> 00:01:03,897
That the end of the map reveals.

19
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:06,677
Is only legendary.

20
00:01:06,760 --> 00:01:10,117
Until someone proves it real.

21
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:12,557
Through it all?

22
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:14,497
Through all the trouble and times.

23
00:01:14,580 --> 00:01:16,817
Through the heartache
and through the pain.

24
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:21,380
Know that I will be there to stand by you.

25
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:24,240
Just like I know you'll stand by me.

26
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:30,660
So come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

27
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:36,040
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

28
00:01:37,160 --> 00:01:42,500
There's always room for you
if you want to be my friend.

29
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:46,880
We are, we are on a cruise.

30
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:49,637
We are.

31
00:01:49,720 --> 00:01:54,060
So you're a pirate?

32
00:01:54,840 --> 00:01:55,670
Uh-huh.

33
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:57,517
Is that why you went and did a crazy thing

34
00:01:57,600 --> 00:01:59,817
like shoot a cannonball
into the restaurant?

35
00:01:59,900 --> 00:02:00,957
That was an accident.

36
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:03,637
It was self-defense that
turned into a stray shot.

37
00:02:03,720 --> 00:02:04,840
A stray shot?

38
00:02:05,620 --> 00:02:09,657
In any case, you really don't want
to do anything stupid to this place.

39
00:02:09,740 --> 00:02:12,858
The owner used to be a cook
in a famous pirate fleet.

40
00:02:13,740 --> 00:02:16,820
Oh, so the old man used to be a pirate.

41
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:19,657
The restaurant is everything
to that crazy old man.

42
00:02:19,740 --> 00:02:22,497
It's the only treasure he'll
need for the rest of his life.

43
00:02:22,580 --> 00:02:24,337
He'll do anything to protect it,

44
00:02:24,420 --> 00:02:26,517
on top of which all of the
cooks who joined him out of

45
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:30,117
respect and admiration are just
as hot-headed as any pirate.

46
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:33,417
Which helps, since pirates are always
coming and going out of this place.

47
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:34,860
Yeah, notice that.

48
00:02:35,220 --> 00:02:37,520
This is a really wild restaurant, huh?

49
00:02:39,140 --> 00:02:39,970
So true.

50
00:02:40,053 --> 00:02:41,737
And this is how it is every day.

51
00:02:41,820 --> 00:02:43,997
It's gotten so bad that
customers are coming here

52
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:46,937
just to watch fights between
the cooks and the pirates.

53
00:02:47,020 --> 00:02:49,937
Every day it's been a new
pirate ship and a new rampage.

54
00:02:50,020 --> 00:02:52,677
It wasn't long till all the
waiters got scared and bailed.

55
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:54,280
Ah, that makes sense.

56
00:02:54,460 --> 00:02:57,837
So that's why the old man wanted
me to work for him for a year.

57
00:02:57,920 --> 00:03:00,117
So, you joining my pirate crew or what?

58
00:03:00,200 --> 00:03:01,600
I'm sorry, but I can't.

59
00:03:01,980 --> 00:03:04,097
There's a reason I have to
work here in the restaurant,

60
00:03:04,180 --> 00:03:06,097
and so I can't just walk away from it.

61
00:03:06,180 --> 00:03:07,780
No way! I don't accept!

62
00:03:08,180 --> 00:03:09,180
You don't accept?

63
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:10,517
It's very simple.

64
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:12,357
I refuse to accept your refusal.

65
00:03:12,440 --> 00:03:13,917
You're a good cook, and I need one,

66
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:16,757
so it's obvious that we
should be pirates together.

67
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:17,837
Listen to what I'm saying.

68
00:03:17,920 --> 00:03:19,037
I can't leave here, all right?

69
00:03:19,120 --> 00:03:22,557
What's your reason for saying I
don't have to tell you anything?

70
00:03:22,640 --> 00:03:25,597
What the but you just
said to listen to you!

71
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:29,037
I told you my answer was no and that's
all you need to hear from me now!

72
00:03:29,120 --> 00:03:32,977
Take your pirate ship and find a cook
someplace else before I cut you up, Straw Hat!

73
00:03:33,060 --> 00:03:34,413
You listen to me, jerk!

74
00:03:35,020 --> 00:03:37,957
No one makes fun of my Straw Hat
unless they're ready for a beating.

75
00:03:38,040 --> 00:03:39,460
I'm sorry to interrupt

76
00:03:40,140 --> 00:03:41,080
What is it?

77
00:03:41,260 --> 00:03:43,857
My name is Ginny and I'm a
crew member of Don Krieg's

78
00:03:43,940 --> 00:03:47,116
pirate fleet and you say
that you're a pirate yourself

79
00:03:47,580 --> 00:03:48,756
What is it you seek?

80
00:03:48,980 --> 00:03:50,120
Oh, the one piece.

81
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:54,007
And pretty soon, I'm going to
sail the Grand Line and find it.

82
00:03:57,080 --> 00:03:59,317
Well, you can't have
been seeking it for long.

83
00:03:59,400 --> 00:04:02,917
If you don't even have a cook yet,
your crew can't be all that big.

84
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:04,817
Nope, he's only the fifth member.

85
00:04:04,900 --> 00:04:06,997
I told you I'm not
going, so don't count me!

86
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:10,737
You seem like a nice kid, so let me
give you some friendly advice, okay?

87
00:04:10,820 --> 00:04:13,237
The Grand Line is a
place you want to avoid.

88
00:04:13,320 --> 00:04:15,717
You're still young, there's
no need to rush into anything.

89
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:19,620
Remember, the Grand Line is one
small part of this entire ocean.

90
00:04:19,880 --> 00:04:21,297
If you want to be a real pirate,

91
00:04:21,380 --> 00:04:25,157
there are plenty of other places
out here on the seas to explore.

92
00:04:25,240 --> 00:04:26,680
Hmm, I see.

93
00:04:27,020 --> 00:04:30,117
Well, why don't you just tell me
what to avoid in the Grand Line now?

94
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:31,030
I can't.

95
00:04:31,113 --> 00:04:32,320
I don't know anything.

96
00:04:32,660 --> 00:04:34,340
I don't understand it.

97
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:36,680
And that is why I fear it.

98
00:04:37,600 --> 00:04:42,280
For being a crew member of Don Krieg's,
you're a pretty wimpy pirate. Hmm?

99
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:44,100
Who's Don Krieg?

100
00:04:53,020 --> 00:04:54,917
The appetizer for table three is ready.

101
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:55,830
Yeah.

102
00:04:55,913 --> 00:04:57,477
Well, you're gonna have
to take it out yourself.

103
00:04:57,560 --> 00:04:58,857
The last waiter's gone.

104
00:04:58,940 --> 00:05:00,917
You think more of them will be coming?

105
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:02,097
Patty. Who knows?

106
00:05:02,180 --> 00:05:06,797
I heard the guy you beat up earlier in
the restaurant was one of Don Krieg's men.

107
00:05:06,880 --> 00:05:09,197
I don't think that will make
the rest of them very happy.

108
00:05:09,280 --> 00:05:12,117
I don't care whose man he was.

109
00:05:12,200 --> 00:05:14,157
All I'm saying is the stories I've heard.

110
00:05:14,240 --> 00:05:15,957
say Don Krieg is the strongest,

111
00:05:16,040 --> 00:05:18,437
fiercest, and most evil pirate
in this part of the ocean.

112
00:05:18,520 --> 00:05:19,350
He is.

113
00:05:22,680 --> 00:05:26,197
On these waters, his grip of
fear reaches far and wide.

114
00:05:26,280 --> 00:05:31,200
He commands over 50 pirate captains, one
of the largest pirate fleets ever seen.

115
00:05:34,080 --> 00:05:36,760
He is truly a monster.

116
00:05:37,080 --> 00:05:38,400
He doesn't scare me.

117
00:05:39,900 --> 00:05:44,429
I've heard that his extraordinary fleet
of ships has more than 5,000 pirates.

118
00:05:46,340 --> 00:05:50,517
this could be bad for boss if if
that guy you beat up goes to don

119
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:54,017
krieg and tells him what you did
and he sends just one ship there

120
00:05:54,100 --> 00:05:57,537
won't be enough of us to fight
them off we'll be crushed like a

121
00:05:57,620 --> 00:06:01,561
grape under an elephant and left
to sink to the bottom of the ocean

122
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:04,897
you're saying i should
have just served them so

123
00:06:04,980 --> 00:06:07,037
we could experience our
great customer service

124
00:06:07,120 --> 00:06:09,317
and meals for free you
don't think that would have

125
00:06:09,400 --> 00:06:12,224
been rude to the other
damn crooks who pay money

126
00:06:13,940 --> 00:06:17,877
I would never stoop that
low This is the Baratier The

127
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:21,019
fighting cooks have a
reputation to uphold Don't we?

128
00:06:21,180 --> 00:06:22,337
I'd never ruin that.

129
00:06:22,420 --> 00:06:24,217
I don't care who that pirate cries to!

130
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:25,537
Let them send their ships.

131
00:06:25,620 --> 00:06:26,717
I'll fight them all off!

132
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:29,297
If you're scared, quit and
let the real cooks work.

133
00:06:29,380 --> 00:06:30,777
Don't you dare say that to me!

134
00:06:30,860 --> 00:06:32,817
I'm tired of all the
big talk you spit out.

135
00:06:32,900 --> 00:06:34,637
Which is why all the waiters jumped ship.

136
00:06:34,720 --> 00:06:38,640
Everything that's happening now
is all your fault, Patty? Please!

137
00:06:38,840 --> 00:06:42,377
Those waiters were worthless wimps
the moment a customer showed up.

138
00:06:42,460 --> 00:06:43,580
Worthless whips!

139
00:06:44,060 --> 00:06:45,100
Go for it!

140
00:06:45,300 --> 00:06:46,535
Take him out, Carney!

141
00:06:46,880 --> 00:06:48,821
It doesn't stand a chance, Patty!

142
00:06:49,420 --> 00:06:51,008
All right, what's all this?

143
00:06:51,360 --> 00:06:52,960
Get back to work already!

144
00:06:53,200 --> 00:06:54,380
Yes, boss, Sam!

145
00:06:56,340 --> 00:06:57,380
So long, then.

146
00:06:58,040 --> 00:07:00,837
Thanks for the warning, but I'm
still gonna go to the Grand Line.

147
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:01,750
I know.

148
00:07:01,833 --> 00:07:02,960
Do whatever you want.

149
00:07:03,220 --> 00:07:05,257
I'm just a stranger, and I can't stop you!

150
00:07:05,340 --> 00:07:07,257
from going anywhere you want to go.

151
00:07:07,340 --> 00:07:09,752
I just wanted to give you a fair warning.

152
00:07:10,640 --> 00:07:11,617
And to you, chef?

153
00:07:11,700 --> 00:07:16,457
Thank you for everything you saved
my life and I owe you for that.

154
00:07:16,540 --> 00:07:18,677
Your cooking skills are
the best I've ever seen.

155
00:07:18,760 --> 00:07:21,117
I hope to come back again sometime.

156
00:07:21,200 --> 00:07:23,097
I'll have a seat for you.

157
00:07:23,180 --> 00:07:24,177
Sure, boy.

158
00:07:24,260 --> 00:07:25,417
Get up here right now!

159
00:07:25,500 --> 00:07:28,697
Boss, you're hard to find.

160
00:07:28,780 --> 00:07:34,617
Hey, Gain? Go.

161
00:07:34,700 --> 00:07:36,757
Sorry.

162
00:07:36,840 --> 00:07:39,377
You'll probably get yelled at or fired?

163
00:07:39,460 --> 00:07:41,754
because you gave me that food for free.

164
00:07:43,620 --> 00:07:44,450
Whatever.

165
00:07:53,180 --> 00:07:54,437
Now there's not proof, sir.

166
00:07:54,520 --> 00:07:56,814
There's no way for me to get yelled at.

167
00:08:00,180 --> 00:08:02,415
Try not to get caught again, you hear?

168
00:08:02,900 --> 00:08:04,620
Thank you again, Chef Sanji.

169
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:06,840
I will never forget your kindness.

170
00:08:09,980 --> 00:08:11,100
Sanji! Chorboy!

171
00:08:11,440 --> 00:08:13,020
Get back to work already!

172
00:08:13,860 --> 00:08:14,690
Hey!

173
00:08:14,773 --> 00:08:15,620
Table 3 is ready!

174
00:08:19,220 --> 00:08:20,050
Hey, guys!

175
00:08:20,133 --> 00:08:23,377
My name's Luffy and I'm gonna
be the new Chorboy around here!

176
00:08:23,460 --> 00:08:24,872
Nice to meet all of you!

177
00:08:39,280 --> 00:08:41,045
What happened to that dessert?

178
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:45,257
Which one of us was supposed to make that?

179
00:08:45,340 --> 00:08:46,837
It was supposed to be him.

180
00:08:46,920 --> 00:08:48,357
I don't have time to make that.

181
00:08:48,440 --> 00:08:49,270
I'm too busy.

182
00:08:49,353 --> 00:08:50,877
You're too busy being injured.

183
00:08:50,960 --> 00:08:52,900
Say that again. I dare you.

184
00:08:54,900 --> 00:08:56,797
Don't you sit there picking your nose?

185
00:08:56,880 --> 00:08:58,497
Go wash the dishes or something.

186
00:08:58,580 --> 00:08:59,410
Right now.

187
00:08:59,760 --> 00:09:01,320
Has anyone seen Sanji?

188
00:09:02,060 --> 00:09:04,017
I think I saw him hitting on a customer.

189
00:09:04,100 --> 00:09:04,930
Again?

190
00:09:05,013 --> 00:09:06,697
I wish Boss Zef would get rid of him.

191
00:09:06,780 --> 00:09:10,537
It's bad enough he's the Zeus chef, but
he's never in the kitchen doing his job.

192
00:09:10,620 --> 00:09:12,197
I think we're stuck with him.

193
00:09:12,280 --> 00:09:14,057
He's worked here longer than any of us.

194
00:09:14,140 --> 00:09:17,617
He was working the kitchen and the
dining room even before I started.

195
00:09:17,700 --> 00:09:19,994
Yeah, but even so, I just don't get it.

196
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:23,217
Why does he stay here when he
and Boss Zephyr always fighting?

197
00:09:23,300 --> 00:09:25,476
I think he wants to be the head chef.

198
00:09:26,100 --> 00:09:26,930
Huh?

199
00:09:27,860 --> 00:09:29,100
Huh? Hmm?

200
00:09:30,860 --> 00:09:31,690
Chore boy!

201
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:35,577
Just how many of these dishes have
you gone and broken into tiny pieces?

202
00:09:35,660 --> 00:09:36,490
You know what?

203
00:09:36,780 --> 00:09:38,640
I forgot to count! Aw, man!

204
00:09:38,760 --> 00:09:40,737
I wasn't being serious, you idiot!

205
00:09:40,820 --> 00:09:42,077
Why are you breaking them?

206
00:09:42,160 --> 00:09:44,820
Stop screwing around
and clean up your mess!

207
00:09:45,140 --> 00:09:46,180
That I can do!

208
00:09:48,080 --> 00:09:48,910
Stop!

209
00:09:49,060 --> 00:09:50,236
Don't take the food!

210
00:09:50,480 --> 00:09:51,697
What's wrong with you?

211
00:09:51,780 --> 00:09:53,309
That was a perfect entree!

212
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:55,500
Yep, pretty tasty!

213
00:10:00,460 --> 00:10:06,300
Why don't we have you take
orders in the dining room?

214
00:10:06,780 --> 00:10:08,977
Just ask the customers
what they want to eat.

215
00:10:09,060 --> 00:10:10,354
Is that simple enough?

216
00:10:10,580 --> 00:10:11,410
Yes.

217
00:10:11,540 --> 00:10:13,600
These chores sure are boring.

218
00:10:13,900 --> 00:10:16,357
I wonder if Kobe got tired
of all this work, too.

219
00:10:16,440 --> 00:10:17,270
Chore boy!

220
00:10:17,620 --> 00:10:18,450
Ugh!

221
00:10:18,533 --> 00:10:19,477
What are you doing?

222
00:10:19,560 --> 00:10:21,617
We heard you had to work
here for a whole year.

223
00:10:21,700 --> 00:10:24,277
Is that okay if we redraw
the flag for our ship?

224
00:10:24,360 --> 00:10:26,897
You're eating all this
delicious food without me?

225
00:10:26,980 --> 00:10:28,437
What kind of crew are you?

226
00:10:28,520 --> 00:10:29,957
Who could you do this to me?

227
00:10:30,040 --> 00:10:30,870
Hold on.

228
00:10:30,953 --> 00:10:33,446
I think that's our
business, isn't that right?

229
00:10:34,080 --> 00:10:35,480
Take this. Oh, boy.

230
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:37,647
This is going to be so good.

231
00:10:38,400 --> 00:10:41,457
You know, I have to say the food
here really is quite delicious.

232
00:10:41,540 --> 00:10:42,700
Good stuff.

233
00:10:43,720 --> 00:10:44,680
Yes, it is.

234
00:10:45,680 --> 00:10:48,237
I feel bad for you, but...

235
00:10:48,320 --> 00:10:50,496
You should be drinking this yourself!

236
00:10:52,880 --> 00:10:55,060
I can't believe you did that!

237
00:10:55,280 --> 00:10:57,692
Yeah, well, I can't believe you did that!

238
00:10:58,760 --> 00:11:00,400
Oh, that was nasty!

239
00:11:07,320 --> 00:11:08,700
Aren't they quaint?

240
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:11,353
I wonder if that's the rest of his crew.

241
00:11:16,840 --> 00:11:18,428
Finish pouring it yourself.

242
00:11:18,820 --> 00:11:23,840
Oh, dear Ocean, thank you for this treasure
you have shared from your depths. Huh?

243
00:11:24,160 --> 00:11:25,780
Ah, yes, my love.

244
00:11:25,940 --> 00:11:28,457
I can't bear this hardship
of loving you from afar.

245
00:11:28,540 --> 00:11:29,716
It is too difficult.

246
00:11:30,060 --> 00:11:33,277
I am now prepared to sail to the
ends of the earth as a pirate!

247
00:11:33,360 --> 00:11:35,177
If it means someone of your rare beauty?

248
00:11:35,260 --> 00:11:36,920
will be by my side.

249
00:11:38,420 --> 00:11:40,660
To be together sailing the seas.

250
00:11:40,980 --> 00:11:43,840
But how tragic a great
obstacle blocks our way.

251
00:11:44,660 --> 00:11:47,160
That great obstacle would be me, right?

252
00:11:47,780 --> 00:11:48,610
Sanji.

253
00:11:48,860 --> 00:11:50,080
Ah, stupid geezer.

254
00:11:50,340 --> 00:11:53,017
This is an opportunity
you don't want to pass up.

255
00:11:53,100 --> 00:11:55,217
Why not join them and become a pirate?

256
00:11:55,300 --> 00:11:58,182
I have no need to keep
you here at my restaurant.

257
00:12:14,800 --> 00:12:15,777
I see.

258
00:12:15,860 --> 00:12:20,700
This cook saved your life, and you
were able to return here to us.

259
00:12:22,580 --> 00:12:24,900
Is that what you're saying, Ginny?

260
00:12:26,380 --> 00:12:32,420
Yes, but you see, I had no idea the main
ship was in this condition, Don Krieg.

261
00:12:33,360 --> 00:12:34,190
No idea.

262
00:12:34,560 --> 00:12:35,680
So what now?

263
00:12:38,300 --> 00:12:41,920
Now I believe I'll take you to
the sea restaurant, Baratier.

264
00:12:46,700 --> 00:12:48,100
Hey, listen, pal.

265
00:12:48,320 --> 00:12:50,340
I'm the Zeus chef in this place.

266
00:12:50,620 --> 00:12:53,149
What do you mean you
don't need me anymore?

267
00:12:53,420 --> 00:12:55,655
You fight with customers all the time.

268
00:12:55,840 --> 00:12:58,857
You flirt with every woman
under 80 who walks through here.

269
00:12:58,940 --> 00:13:00,837
You can't even cook a decent meal.

270
00:13:00,920 --> 00:13:04,100
You're worth less to me
than the chum after brunch.

271
00:13:04,520 --> 00:13:05,617
That's what I mean.

272
00:13:05,700 --> 00:13:07,400
So, uh...

273
00:13:10,240 --> 00:13:14,697
Oh, and let's not forget about how the other
cooks avoid you like you were poisoned.

274
00:13:14,780 --> 00:13:19,260
So just run off and be a pirate or
whatever, but get out of this restaurant.

275
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:22,140
That's how it is?

276
00:13:23,280 --> 00:13:27,868
You shoot off at the mouth and expect
that I'm just going to take it, old man?

277
00:13:28,720 --> 00:13:31,220
I could blow off everything you said,

278
00:13:31,360 --> 00:13:36,220
but I won't listen to anyone trash my
cooking I'm staying here as a Zeus chef,

279
00:13:36,460 --> 00:13:37,680
and that's final.

280
00:13:37,960 --> 00:13:39,040
You hear me?

281
00:13:39,520 --> 00:13:43,285
What do you think you're doing
grabbing your boss by the collar?

282
00:13:43,880 --> 00:13:44,997
You can

283
00:13:45,080 --> 00:13:52,080
try

284
00:13:52,720 --> 00:13:53,780
to kick me out

285
00:13:54,300 --> 00:13:55,720
But I'm here to stay.

286
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:57,882
I'm not going anywhere, old man.

287
00:13:58,360 --> 00:14:00,057
Not till you're dead and gone.

288
00:14:00,140 --> 00:14:00,970
Dead?

289
00:14:01,053 --> 00:14:04,411
I got another hundred years of
kicking your ass left in me.

290
00:14:04,500 --> 00:14:07,080
He's always got to have
the last word. See?

291
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:08,177
He said it's cool.

292
00:14:08,260 --> 00:14:09,417
Now you can become a pirate.

293
00:14:09,500 --> 00:14:10,330
Shut up!

294
00:14:11,160 --> 00:14:12,120
My apologies.

295
00:14:12,620 --> 00:14:17,400
I hope I can make it up to you with this
delightful fruit Macedonia, my princess.

296
00:14:17,780 --> 00:14:19,100
Wow, you're too kind.

297
00:14:19,380 --> 00:14:21,020
It looks wonderful. Good.

298
00:14:21,340 --> 00:14:23,057
Hey, don't forget about us, Mr.

299
00:14:23,140 --> 00:14:23,970
Casanova.

300
00:14:24,053 --> 00:14:26,017
We'd better get some
kind of an apology, too!

301
00:14:26,100 --> 00:14:28,806
This tea should be more
than adequate for you.

302
00:14:29,120 --> 00:14:30,817
In fact, you should be thanking me.

303
00:14:30,900 --> 00:14:31,730
What?

304
00:14:31,813 --> 00:14:32,643
You want to fight?

305
00:14:32,726 --> 00:14:33,907
You're going to regret this!

306
00:14:34,060 --> 00:14:35,300
Take him out, Zoro!

307
00:14:35,660 --> 00:14:36,700
You take him out.

308
00:14:37,180 --> 00:14:38,060
Stop it!

309
00:14:38,220 --> 00:14:39,637
Please don't fight because of me!

310
00:14:39,720 --> 00:14:40,900
Of course, my dear.

311
00:14:41,040 --> 00:14:42,477
Who said it was about you?

312
00:14:42,560 --> 00:14:46,820
I wanted to tell you that all of
the food here is just delicious.

313
00:14:47,180 --> 00:14:49,474
But it's a little too expensive for me.

314
00:14:49,700 --> 00:14:50,920
Relax, it's free!

315
00:14:51,500 --> 00:14:52,330
Oh, thank you!

316
00:14:52,960 --> 00:14:54,960
You guys still got to pay, though.

317
00:14:55,380 --> 00:14:57,460
How very generous of you.

318
00:14:59,540 --> 00:15:01,560
What are you sitting around for?

319
00:15:02,140 --> 00:15:05,040
You're not here to lounge around. Right.

320
00:15:37,140 --> 00:15:37,970
It's them.

321
00:15:38,053 --> 00:15:38,883
They're here.

322
00:15:38,966 --> 00:15:40,917
The hourglasses mean our time is up.

323
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:43,297
What are we gonna do?

324
00:15:43,380 --> 00:15:45,477
Now that flag means death.

325
00:15:45,560 --> 00:15:46,817
There's no doubt.

326
00:15:46,900 --> 00:15:48,777
It belongs to the ruler of the east.

327
00:15:48,860 --> 00:15:51,280
Blue Don Krieg!

328
00:16:06,660 --> 00:16:07,490
But why?

329
00:16:07,573 --> 00:16:09,777
Why have the creek pirates come here?

330
00:16:09,860 --> 00:16:11,297
I told you.

331
00:16:11,380 --> 00:16:13,017
I knew those goons would show up.

332
00:16:13,100 --> 00:16:13,930
Now.

333
00:16:14,013 --> 00:16:15,137
Are you gonna get rid
of those guys or what?

334
00:16:15,220 --> 00:16:16,217
This can't be real.

335
00:16:16,300 --> 00:16:17,857
He's got a whole fleet to command.

336
00:16:17,940 --> 00:16:21,477
Why would Tang Creek come here
to get revenge for just one man?

337
00:16:21,560 --> 00:16:23,337
I mean, doesn't he have
anything better to do?

338
00:16:23,420 --> 00:16:24,517
He's here, all right.

339
00:16:24,600 --> 00:16:26,737
We're not imagining that ship, are we?

340
00:16:26,820 --> 00:16:30,317
Guys, don't panic, but I think
this is our cue to leave right now.

341
00:16:30,400 --> 00:16:32,694
Look at the sheer size of that galleon.

342
00:16:39,880 --> 00:16:41,620
What a huge ship.

343
00:16:41,900 --> 00:16:44,917
You think Ginny came back to
repay you for your kindness?

344
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:46,740
I seriously doubt that's it.

345
00:16:47,360 --> 00:16:48,536
It's something else.

346
00:16:58,180 --> 00:16:59,120
Hey, look!

347
00:16:59,360 --> 00:17:00,600
Yeah, there's Shamp.

348
00:17:07,980 --> 00:17:09,320
Whoa, what'd they do?

349
00:17:09,480 --> 00:17:11,237
Sail through a hurricane or something?

350
00:17:11,320 --> 00:17:14,202
It doesn't seem like damage
inflicted by cannons.

351
00:17:14,680 --> 00:17:17,820
In fact, it doesn't look man-made at all.

352
00:17:18,660 --> 00:17:21,020
Then maybe it was a tornado hurricane.

353
00:17:22,320 --> 00:17:23,460
There he is.

354
00:17:47,660 --> 00:17:53,397
I beg you I need food and water.

355
00:17:53,480 --> 00:17:55,177
We have money.

356
00:17:55,260 --> 00:17:56,720
Lots of money.

357
00:17:59,040 --> 00:18:00,920
No, this can't be.

358
00:18:01,220 --> 00:18:03,137
Where's the death and destruction?

359
00:18:03,220 --> 00:18:07,340
Is this really the Don Krieg,
Commodore of the Grand Pirate Fleet?

360
00:18:08,160 --> 00:18:09,700
Guess he's hungry.

361
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:15,740
Uh, uh, uh, uh,

362
00:18:16,380 --> 00:18:17,220
C-Captain!

363
00:18:18,060 --> 00:18:19,700
Uh, Don Krieg!

364
00:18:21,880 --> 00:18:23,060
Please help him!

365
00:18:23,260 --> 00:18:25,617
Our captain is on the brink of starvation!

366
00:18:25,700 --> 00:18:26,840
He could die!

367
00:18:27,620 --> 00:18:30,208
He hasn't had a single
bite to eat for days.

368
00:18:30,420 --> 00:18:32,949
He'll die if he doesn't
get some food soon.

369
00:18:40,540 --> 00:18:41,440
This is great!

370
00:18:41,640 --> 00:18:43,577
I haven't laughed that
hard in a long time!

371
00:18:43,660 --> 00:18:46,600
The great Don Creek kneeling before us.

372
00:18:46,780 --> 00:18:48,020
We have some money.

373
00:18:48,260 --> 00:18:50,017
We're here as customers this time.

374
00:18:50,100 --> 00:18:52,177
Do you really think I'm that stupid?

375
00:18:52,260 --> 00:18:54,477
Hey, get a hold of the Marines right away.

376
00:18:54,560 --> 00:18:55,390
What?

377
00:18:55,473 --> 00:18:57,437
He's finally weak enough to be captured.

378
00:18:57,520 --> 00:18:58,637
This may never happen again,

379
00:18:58,720 --> 00:19:02,602
and I'm not going to ruin it by
helping him get his strength back.

380
00:19:02,740 --> 00:19:03,570
He's right.

381
00:19:03,653 --> 00:19:05,697
Who knows what he'll do if
he gets on his feet again.

382
00:19:05,780 --> 00:19:07,340
He's done terrible things.

383
00:19:07,620 --> 00:19:09,897
And as soon as he's up,
he'll keep on doing them.

384
00:19:09,980 --> 00:19:11,540
I say we let him starve.

385
00:19:12,300 --> 00:19:16,277
Once he's back to normal, he'll kill
every last person in this restaurant.

386
00:19:16,360 --> 00:19:19,242
He won't get so much as
a glass of water from me.

387
00:19:20,480 --> 00:19:22,620
I won't do anything.

388
00:19:24,760 --> 00:19:26,860
I won't do anything.

389
00:19:27,620 --> 00:19:31,840
Once I eat, I promise I'll leave quietly.

390
00:19:32,300 --> 00:19:35,340
So please, be merciful and help me.

391
00:19:35,680 --> 00:19:37,840
You're a king, Dunkrieg. Stop it.

392
00:19:38,220 --> 00:19:40,257
Please don't reduce yourself to this.

393
00:19:40,340 --> 00:19:43,580
You're better than a
common beggar, please sir.

394
00:19:43,760 --> 00:19:45,080
What about your pride?

395
00:19:45,360 --> 00:19:46,300
I've promised

396
00:19:47,900 --> 00:19:50,460
Please I'll take the scraps.

397
00:19:50,820 --> 00:19:52,440
I'll take anything

398
00:19:53,400 --> 00:19:54,230
Anything

399
00:19:57,540 --> 00:19:58,370
Don

400
00:20:02,240 --> 00:20:07,120
Yeah, boo-hoo for the cruel
pirate hey step aside Paddy?

401
00:20:17,080 --> 00:20:17,910
Sanji!

402
00:20:21,280 --> 00:20:23,280
Here's something for your captain.

403
00:20:26,840 --> 00:20:28,160
Thank you, Sanji.

404
00:20:34,020 --> 00:20:35,000
Thank you.

405
00:20:46,240 --> 00:20:49,237
You dimwit get that food
away from him right now!

406
00:20:49,320 --> 00:20:52,157
Don't you realize he's a cold
heartless killing machine?

407
00:20:52,240 --> 00:20:54,557
This is the man known as the ruler of the

408
00:20:54,640 --> 00:20:57,346
east blue the most
treacherous of all pirates!

409
00:20:58,860 --> 00:21:02,177
It all started back in prison he pretended

410
00:21:02,260 --> 00:21:04,757
to be a marine and when
he decided to declare

411
00:21:04,840 --> 00:21:07,177
his pirate ambitions he took command of a

412
00:21:07,260 --> 00:21:09,848
marine vessel by killing
the senior officer!

413
00:21:11,180 --> 00:21:13,897
He would raise the marine
flag to enter ports!

414
00:21:13,980 --> 00:21:17,677
Then lay waste to the unsuspecting
cities and passenger ships there!

415
00:21:17,760 --> 00:21:20,877
He even showed the white flag
before attacking enemy ships!

416
00:21:20,960 --> 00:21:23,660
He did anything to secure victory!

417
00:21:25,540 --> 00:21:27,377
That guy fights dirty!

418
00:21:27,460 --> 00:21:30,257
He's also unmatched in physical combat!

419
00:21:30,340 --> 00:21:32,540
You think he'll just leave us alone?

420
00:21:32,800 --> 00:21:34,517
Look, I've got news for you.

421
00:21:34,600 --> 00:21:38,097
That's not possible with a
bloodthirsty killer like him!

422
00:21:38,180 --> 00:21:40,180
He deserves death!

423
00:21:40,640 --> 00:21:41,580
Thanks!

424
00:21:57,160 --> 00:21:58,560
Sanji!

425
00:22:08,180 --> 00:22:10,160
This is not what we agreed on.

426
00:22:10,600 --> 00:22:11,940
You gave me your word.

427
00:22:12,140 --> 00:22:16,197
I only brought you here because you
promised that you wouldn't ruin this place.

428
00:22:16,280 --> 00:22:18,300
Or hurt the man who saved us.

429
00:22:22,540 --> 00:22:24,460
Yes, that was delicious.

430
00:22:26,140 --> 00:22:27,820
I feel alive again.

431
00:22:42,200 --> 00:22:43,880
Hey, you see that?

432
00:22:45,760 --> 00:22:47,060
It looks bad.

433
00:22:47,320 --> 00:22:49,157
What do you think is going on in there?

434
00:22:49,240 --> 00:22:50,070
Don't know.

435
00:22:50,153 --> 00:22:50,983
Let's go inside and see.

436
00:22:51,066 --> 00:22:51,896
What?

437
00:22:51,979 --> 00:22:52,809
Are you serious?

438
00:22:54,520 --> 00:22:56,620
This is a pretty good ship.

439
00:22:57,280 --> 00:22:59,560
I believe that I'll take it.

440
00:23:03,460 --> 00:23:04,290
Right.

441
00:23:04,373 --> 00:23:05,203
I see.

442
00:23:14,440 --> 00:23:17,120
As you can all see, my ship is a wreck.

443
00:23:17,840 --> 00:23:20,257
Naturally, I'll be needing a nice new one.

444
00:23:20,340 --> 00:23:25,780
After a few small chores, every last one
of you will leave the ship. What? No!

445
00:23:26,280 --> 00:23:29,580
Don Krieg, you promised! Please!

446
00:23:32,780 --> 00:23:35,940
There are about a hundred
men left on board my ship.

447
00:23:36,260 --> 00:23:37,920
All are weak with hunger.

448
00:23:38,180 --> 00:23:40,060
And many are seriously wounded.

449
00:23:40,480 --> 00:23:45,560
If you value your lives, you will prepare
food and water for every last one of them.

450
00:23:46,140 --> 00:23:49,020
I've lost too many men to hunger already.

451
00:23:51,440 --> 00:23:52,270
Water!

452
00:23:56,000 --> 00:23:58,140
Bring them over! Immediately!

453
00:23:58,720 --> 00:24:01,560
You're telling us to
feed our executioners?

454
00:24:01,700 --> 00:24:03,759
Do you hear how stupid that sounds?

455
00:24:03,860 --> 00:24:04,760
We refuse!

456
00:24:05,700 --> 00:24:06,757
You refuse?

457
00:24:06,840 --> 00:24:09,340
Jews, I wasn't asking you.

458
00:24:09,520 --> 00:24:11,920
Now make no mistake, you wretched cook.

459
00:24:12,120 --> 00:24:13,820
I'm not placing an order.

460
00:24:14,020 --> 00:24:15,680
I am giving you one.

461
00:24:15,900 --> 00:24:17,380
Do I make myself clear?

462
00:24:17,600 --> 00:24:18,880
Don't defy me!

463
00:24:27,120 --> 00:24:27,950
Sanji.

464
00:24:29,560 --> 00:24:31,260
Sanji. Sorry.

465
00:24:31,600 --> 00:24:34,897
I didn't mean for this to happen. You see?

466
00:24:34,980 --> 00:24:38,451
Look what you brought on this
restaurant you stupid bastard

467
00:24:56,080 --> 00:24:58,680
Hey, where do you think you're going?

468
00:25:00,840 --> 00:25:02,060
To the kitchen

469
00:25:02,880 --> 00:25:06,056
Looks like I'll be cooking
a hundred more meals today.

470
00:25:07,040 --> 00:25:08,480
Sanji! Sanji!

471
00:25:09,180 --> 00:25:10,010
What?

472
00:25:10,093 --> 00:25:11,020
Are you crazy?

473
00:25:12,540 --> 00:25:13,370
Good.

474
00:25:13,453 --> 00:25:14,400
Hop to it.

475
00:25:19,420 --> 00:25:20,960
Tell me the truth, Sanji!

476
00:25:21,080 --> 00:25:22,417
Are you his spy or something?

477
00:25:22,500 --> 00:25:24,837
We can't let you go
anywhere near that kitchen.

478
00:25:24,920 --> 00:25:27,038
We're fed up with you acting insane.

479
00:25:29,420 --> 00:25:30,420
All right.

480
00:25:31,640 --> 00:25:33,300
Stop me if you wish.

481
00:25:37,120 --> 00:25:38,100
I know.

482
00:25:39,460 --> 00:25:43,340
It's no secret that Don Krieg
is a terrible, ruthless man.

483
00:25:45,580 --> 00:25:47,580
But that doesn't matter to me.

484
00:25:48,820 --> 00:25:50,200
It doesn't matter.

485
00:25:51,840 --> 00:25:55,820
After we feed all these men, who
knows what's going to happen?

486
00:25:56,220 --> 00:25:59,297
I am just a simple cook,
no more and no less.

487
00:25:59,380 --> 00:26:02,720
If someone's going hungry,
it's my duty to feed them.

488
00:26:02,900 --> 00:26:03,980
That's all I know.

489
00:26:05,800 --> 00:26:06,980
What do you say?

490
00:26:07,880 --> 00:26:09,020
Is that wrong?

491
00:26:17,260 --> 00:26:18,090
Penny!

492
00:26:18,360 --> 00:26:20,220
Hey, somebody grab him!

493
00:26:21,100 --> 00:26:26,180
You bring free food to the bums I kick
out of this place over and over again.

494
00:26:27,060 --> 00:26:30,577
And I'm not about to argue over who's
right in that particular situation,

495
00:26:30,660 --> 00:26:33,484
but this time you're just
flat out wrong, Sanji.

496
00:26:33,680 --> 00:26:36,268
I can't let you do
things like that anymore.

497
00:26:36,600 --> 00:26:38,600
We're going to protect this place.

498
00:26:38,820 --> 00:26:41,237
Fortunately, we've got
numbers on our side.

499
00:26:41,320 --> 00:26:44,614
It is Don Krieg, but what
could he do against all of us?

500
00:26:46,140 --> 00:26:49,920
At a joint like this, pirate
scumbags come and go all day.

501
00:26:50,220 --> 00:26:53,380
We're fully prepared to
serve any kind of customer.

502
00:26:53,780 --> 00:26:54,677
Is that...

503
00:26:54,760 --> 00:26:57,600
I really hope you saved
some room for dessert.

504
00:26:57,980 --> 00:27:01,180
Cause I have a secret recipe. Huh?

505
00:27:01,640 --> 00:27:03,660
That is truly to die for!

506
00:27:04,140 --> 00:27:05,520
Open wide!

507
00:27:06,220 --> 00:27:08,460
Here comes the meatball of doom!

508
00:27:26,480 --> 00:27:27,310
Don!

509
00:27:32,500 --> 00:27:34,300
I might have broken the door.

510
00:27:34,600 --> 00:27:36,877
I sure hope Zef doesn't yell at me again.

511
00:27:36,960 --> 00:27:40,489
They might go easy on you for
saving the restaurant and all.

512
00:27:41,440 --> 00:27:45,381
So what are we going to do about
all the guys left in Krieg's ship?

513
00:27:45,580 --> 00:27:46,410
Fry them!

514
00:27:46,493 --> 00:27:48,920
Cover it and batter and
fry the entire thing!

515
00:27:49,400 --> 00:27:51,760
Are you a chef or a comedian?

516
00:27:52,700 --> 00:27:55,120
because your jokes are lame.

517
00:27:56,940 --> 00:27:59,480
And that dessert was terrible.

518
00:27:59,860 --> 00:28:01,840
The worst I ever had.

519
00:28:06,840 --> 00:28:08,340
So die!

520
00:28:15,600 --> 00:28:17,340
